<ansi fg="black-bold">.:</ansi> <ansi fg="magenta">Help for </ansi><ansi fg="skill">enchanting</ansi> (skill)

Enchantments are not forged — they are grown. In Chrysalis, living mutations dwell
within carefully crafted settings, binding themselves to your weapons and armor
through long use and shared struggle. The skill is governed by <ansi fg="yellow">Perception</ansi>,
since coaxing a mutation to bond with an item requires attunement and patience.

<ansi fg="yellow">━━━ How Enchantments Work ━━━</ansi>

An enchanted item claims a portion of your life force. You will see a dark section
in your vital bars — that energy belongs to the enchantment now. As you adventure
with the enchanted item, the bond deepens. You will know when it changes — the
item itself will tell you.

Removing an enchantment is possible at an enchanting circle, but the separation is
not clean. Expect to feel weakened for a time.

<ansi fg="yellow">━━━ Requirements ━━━</ansi>

  Station:   An <ansi fg="yellow">enchanting_circle</ansi> must be in the room with you.
  Materials: Chrysalis settings and the item you wish to enchant.
             Chrysalis settings are created through jewelcrafting.

