<ansi fg="yellow">━━━ Enchantment Types ━━━</ansi>

Each enchantment brings a different mutation to bear:

  <ansi fg="yellow">Serpent's Edge</ansi>        A reptilian hunger that sharpens your blade.
  <ansi fg="yellow">Stone Ward</ansi>            The weight and resilience of stone in your defense.
  <ansi fg="yellow">Hawk's Perception</ansi>     Predator's vision that sees through the veil.
  <ansi fg="yellow">Fortified Stance</ansi>      Roots that ground you against all shaking.
  <ansi fg="yellow">Quickened Reflexes</ansi>    Arachnid speed that makes the world slow.
  <ansi fg="yellow">Crystalline Form</ansi>      Gemstone hardness woven into your being.
  <ansi fg="yellow">Apex Predator</ansi>        Primal hunting instinct made manifest.
  <ansi fg="yellow">Unbreakable Bond</ansi>      A fusion of wills — item and bearer as one.

<ansi fg="yellow">━━━ Skill Progression ━━━</ansi>

Enchanting improves through use. Each completed enchantment attempt (success or
failure) has a chance to advance the skill. Enchanting progresses faster per use
than combat skills because enchanting opportunities are less frequent.

There is no trainer for enchanting — practice is the only teacher.

<ansi fg="yellow">━━━ Commands ━━━</ansi>

  <ansi fg="command">craft list</ansi>          Show all recipes, including enchanting ones, with status.
  <ansi fg="command">craft <recipe></ansi>      Begin enchanting an item.
  <ansi fg="command">disenchant <item></ansi>   Remove an enchantment from an equipped item.
  <ansi fg="command">skills</ansi>              Check your current enchanting skill level.

